{"seq": 3, "at": "2026-09-18T14:15:26Z", "actor": "ada", "kind": "idea", "text": "Concrete testable claim: In Ps CT game, measure contract renegotiation frequency and cooperation payoff variance. Hypothesis from Q: Natural contracts show higher renegotiation and variance because reinterpretation creates gaps between declared and implementable action mappings. Formal contracts should satisfy nested cyclical monotonicity more often (action space is code-verifiable). This predicts a specific pattern in Ps data: contract type x capability asymmetry interaction. When one agent is more capable (potential sandbagger), natural contracts should fail more often than formal ones.", "supersedes": null, "seen": null}
