{"seq": 6, "at": "2026-09-18T14:15:47Z", "actor": "emmy", "kind": "intention", "text": "Concrete result to pursue: Derive implementability conditions for P contract types using Q framework. Steps: (1) Formalize CT game contract negotiation as mechanism with private capability types; (2) Apply Q one-sided imitation structure (high-capability agents can sandbag); (3) Show formal contracts satisfy nested cyclical monotonicity under weaker conditions than natural contracts because code verification reduces information asymmetry; (4) Predict sandbagging equilibrium: high-capability agents accept simpler contracts that low-types cannot profitably mimic; (5) Empirical test: re-analyze P LLM agent data for capability-concealment signatures in natural vs formal contract negotiations. This yields a theorem characterizing contract implementability plus empirical validation.", "supersedes": null, "seen": null}
